IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp4-nouns`
IMPORT `cp4-incapacity`
IMPORT `cp4-calendar`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, sections 60, 61 and 62 -- APPLYING FOR A BENEFIT, INTERIM BENEFITS, WHEN PAYMENT IS MADE.
--
-- Section 60 says that no benefit is payable without an application and an approval, when an application is
-- deemed to have been made (post-retirement benefits, waiver for a person of 70 or more, a deceased person's
-- estate, a child's or orphan's death, incapacity), how it is made, and what the Minister does with it. Section
-- 61 lets the Minister approve an interim benefit where the amount cannot yet be fixed. Section 62 says when
-- payment is made and when a benefit is deemed to have become payable.
--
-- Out of range, taken as plain inputs: the persons and the manner "prescribed" (regs 43 and 57, piece cr2);
-- the earnings of section 76.1 (piece cp5); the meaning of "decision-making responsibility" (s 42(1) and the
-- Divorce Act); the Income Tax Act, the Old Age Security Act and the benefits under them (not among the texts).

§ `Section 60 -- application for benefit`

§§ `Section 60(1) to (1.3) -- the application`

-- src:2016 | 60 (1) No benefit is payable to any person under this Act unless an application therefor has been made by him or on his behalf and payment of the benefit has been approved under this Act.
@ref Act s 60(1) (src:2016)
GIVEN `an application for the benefit has been made by the person or on the person's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `payment of the benefit has been approved under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(1) — a benefit is payable to the person` `an application for the benefit has been made by the person or on the person's behalf` `payment of the benefit has been approved under this Act` MEANS
    -- "No benefit is payable ... unless an application therefor has been made ... and payment ... has been approved":
    -- these are the two conditions. An application deemed made under subsections (1.1), (1.3), (8), (9) or (5) counts as made.
        `an application for the benefit has been made by the person or on the person's behalf`
    AND `payment of the benefit has been approved under this Act`

-- src:2017 | Application for post-retirement benefit deemed to be made
-- src:2018 | (1.1) An application for a post-retirement benefit under subsection (1) is deemed to be made on January 1 of the year following the year of the unadjusted pensionable earnings referred to in section 76.1 if
-- src:2019 | (a) the person is a beneficiary of a retirement pension on that day; and
-- src:2020 | (b) the Minister has the information necessary to determine whether a post-retirement benefit is payable to them.
@ref Act s 60(1.1) (src:2018-2020)
GIVEN `the year of the unadjusted pensionable earnings referred to in section 76.1` IS A NUMBER
      `the person is a beneficiary of a retirement pension on that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has the information necessary to determine whether a post-retirement benefit is payable to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 60(1.1) — the day an application for a post-retirement benefit is deemed to be made` `the year of the unadjusted pensionable earnings referred to in section 76.1` `the person is a beneficiary of a retirement pension on that day` `the Minister has the information necessary to determine whether a post-retirement benefit is payable to the person` MEANS
    -- "that day" is January 1 of the year following the year of the earnings.
    IF   `the person is a beneficiary of a retirement pension on that day`
     AND `the Minister has the information necessary to determine whether a post-retirement benefit is payable to the person`
    THEN JUST (YMD (`the year of the unadjusted pensionable earnings referred to in section 76.1` PLUS 1) 1 1)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2021 | Application for retirement pension waived
-- src:2022 | (1.2) The Minister may waive the requirement under subsection (1) for an application for a retirement pension to be made by a person or on their behalf if the Minister is satisfied that
-- src:2023 | (a) the person is a contributor;
-- src:2024 | (b) the person is 70 years old or more; and
-- src:2025 | (c) at least one of the following applies in respect of the person:
-- src:2026 | (i) the person is in receipt of a benefit under this Act, the Old Age Security Act or a provincial pension plan, and
-- src:2027 | (ii) a return of income was filed by the person or on their behalf under the Income Tax Act in respect of the year before the year in which the Minister considers waiving the requirement.
@ref Act s 60(1.2) (src:2022-2027)
GIVEN `the person is a contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Minister considers waiving the requirement` IS A DATE
      `the person is in receipt of a benefit under this Act, the Old Age Security Act or a provincial pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a return of income was filed by the person or on their behalf under the Income Tax Act in respect of the year before the year in which the Minister considers waiving the requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(1.2) — the Minister may waive the requirement for an application for a retirement pension` `the person is a contributor` `date of birth` `the day on which the Minister considers waiving the requirement` `the person is in receipt of a benefit under this Act, the Old Age Security Act or a provincial pension plan` `a return of income was filed by the person or on their behalf under the Income Tax Act in respect of the year before the year in which the Minister considers waiving the requirement` MEANS
    -- "if the Minister is satisfied that": the three paragraphs are the facts of which the Minister must be satisfied.
    -- Paragraph (c) says "at least one of the following applies" and then joins (i) and (ii) with "and": read as
    -- alternatives, as its opening words say (NOTES.md, fork register).
        `the person is a contributor`
    AND `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `date of birth` 70 `the day on which the Minister considers waiving the requirement`
    AND (   `the person is in receipt of a benefit under this Act, the Old Age Security Act or a provincial pension plan`
         OR `a return of income was filed by the person or on their behalf under the Income Tax Act in respect of the year before the year in which the Minister considers waiving the requirement`)

-- src:2028 | Effect of waiver
-- src:2029 | (1.3) If the requirement for an application for a retirement pension is waived, the application is deemed to have been made and received on the day on which the requirement is waived.
@ref Act s 60(1.3) (src:2029)
GIVEN `the requirement for an application for a retirement pension is waived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the requirement is waived` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 60(1.3) — the day the application for a retirement pension is deemed to have been made and received` `the requirement for an application for a retirement pension is waived` `the day on which the requirement is waived` MEANS
    IF `the requirement for an application for a retirement pension is waived`
    THEN JUST `the day on which the requirement is waived`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 60(2) to (5) -- applications after a death`

-- src:2030 | Application for benefit by estate, etc.
-- src:2031 | (2) Notwithstanding anything in this Act, but subject to subsections (2.1) and (2.2), an application for a benefit, other than a death benefit, that would have been payable in respect of a month to a deceased person who, prior to the person’s death, would have been entitled on approval of an application to payment of that benefit under this Act may be approved in respect of that month only if it is made within 12 months after the death of that person by the estate, the representative or heir of that person or by any person that may be prescribed by regulation.
@ref Act s 60(2) (src:2031)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of benefit`
      `the deceased person would, prior to death, have been entitled on approval of an application to payment of the benefit in respect of the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the application is made by the estate, the representative or heir of the deceased person, or by a person prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved in respect of the month` kind `the deceased person would, prior to death, have been entitled on approval of an application to payment of the benefit in respect of the month` `the day of the death` `the day the application is made` `the application is made by the estate, the representative or heir of the deceased person, or by a person prescribed by regulation` MEANS
    -- "an application for a benefit, other than a death benefit"; "within 12 months after the death".
        (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `a death benefit` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND `the deceased person would, prior to death, have been entitled on approval of an application to payment of the benefit in respect of the month`
    AND `a date is within a time limit after a start date` `the day the application is made` `the day of the death` (`a number of months` WITH `number of months` IS 12)
    AND `the application is made by the estate, the representative or heir of the deceased person, or by a person prescribed by regulation`

-- src:2032 | Certain applications may not be approved
-- src:2033 | (2.1) An application referred to in subsection (2) is not to be approved if it is made in respect of a post-retirement disability benefit or, if the application is received after December 31, 1997, a disability pension.
@ref Act s 60(2.1) (src:2033)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of benefit`
      `the day the application is received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(2.1) — an application referred to in subsection (2) is not to be approved` kind `the day the application is received` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a post-retirement disability benefit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a disability pension` THEN `the day the application is received` AT LEAST (YMD 1998 1 1)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:2034 | Restriction — retirement pension
-- src:2035 | (2.2) An application referred to in subsection (2) in respect of a retirement pension may only be approved in respect of a month after the deceased contributor had reached age 70.
@ref Act s 60(2.2) (src:2035)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of benefit`
      `the deceased contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      month IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(2.2) — an application referred to in subsection (2) in respect of a retirement pension may be approved for the month` kind `the deceased contributor's date of birth` month MEANS
    -- "only in respect of a month after the deceased contributor had reached age 70": reaching 70 goes through section 2(2);
    -- a month is after it when the contributor is treated as having reached 70 by the start of the month. Other benefits are not restricted here.
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a retirement pension` THEN `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the deceased contributor's date of birth` 70 (`the month of a date` month)
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:2030 | Application for benefit by estate, etc.
-- src:2031 | (2) Notwithstanding anything in this Act, but subject to subsections (2.1) and (2.2), an application for a benefit, other than a death benefit, that would have been payable in respect of a month to a deceased person who, prior to the person’s death, would have been entitled on approval of an application to payment of that benefit under this Act may be approved in respect of that month only if it is made within 12 months after the death of that person by the estate, the representative or heir of that person or by any person that may be prescribed by regulation.
-- src:2032 | Certain applications may not be approved
-- src:2033 | (2.1) An application referred to in subsection (2) is not to be approved if it is made in respect of a post-retirement disability benefit or, if the application is received after December 31, 1997, a disability pension.
-- src:2034 | Restriction — retirement pension
-- src:2035 | (2.2) An application referred to in subsection (2) in respect of a retirement pension may only be approved in respect of a month after the deceased contributor had reached age 70.
@ref Act s 60(2), (2.1), (2.2) (src:2031-2035)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of benefit`
      `the deceased person would, prior to death, have been entitled on approval of an application to payment of the benefit in respect of the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the day the application is received` IS A DATE
      `the application is made by the estate, the representative or heir of the deceased person, or by a person prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased contributor's date of birth` IS A DATE
      month IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(2) to (2.2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved for the month` kind `the deceased person would, prior to death, have been entitled on approval of an application to payment of the benefit in respect of the month` `the day of the death` `the day the application is made` `the day the application is received` `the application is made by the estate, the representative or heir of the deceased person, or by a person prescribed by regulation` `the deceased contributor's date of birth` month MEANS
        `s 60(2) — an application for a benefit of a deceased person may be approved in respect of the month` kind `the deceased person would, prior to death, have been entitled on approval of an application to payment of the benefit in respect of the month` `the day of the death` `the day the application is made` `the application is made by the estate, the representative or heir of the deceased person, or by a person prescribed by regulation`
    AND (NOT `s 60(2.1) — an application referred to in subsection (2) is not to be approved` kind `the day the application is received`)
    AND `s 60(2.2) — an application referred to in subsection (2) in respect of a retirement pension may be approved for the month` kind `the deceased contributor's date of birth` month

-- src:2036 | Exception
-- src:2037 | (3) If a disabled contributor’s child’s benefit would, if the application had been approved, have been payable to a child of a disabled contributor on application made prior to the death of the child or an orphan’s benefit would, if the application had been approved, have been payable to an orphan of a contributor on application made prior to the death of the orphan and the child or orphan dies after December 31, 1977, not having reached 18 years of age, and no application has been made at the time of the death of the child or orphan, an application may be made within one year after the death by the person or agency having decision-making responsibility in respect of the child or orphan at the time of the death or, if there is at that time no such person or agency, by any person or agency that the Minister may direct.
@ref Act s 60(3) (src:2037)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of benefit`
      `the benefit would, if the application had been approved, have been payable on an application made prior to the death of the child or orphan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the death of the child or orphan` IS A DATE
      `the child's or orphan's date of birth` IS A DATE
      `no application had been made at the time of the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the application is made` IS A DATE
      `the applicant is the person or agency having decision-making responsibility in respect of the child or orphan at the time of the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there was at the time of the death no person or agency having decision-making responsibility` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a person or agency that the Minister has directed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(3) — an application may be made after the death of a child or orphan` kind `the benefit would, if the application had been approved, have been payable on an application made prior to the death of the child or orphan` `the day of the death of the child or orphan` `the child's or orphan's date of birth` `no application had been made at the time of the death` `the day the application is made` `the applicant is the person or agency having decision-making responsibility in respect of the child or orphan at the time of the death` `there was at the time of the death no person or agency having decision-making responsibility` `the applicant is a person or agency that the Minister has directed` MEANS
        (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `a disabled contributor's child's benefit` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `an orphan's benefit` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND `the benefit would, if the application had been approved, have been payable on an application made prior to the death of the child or orphan`
    AND `the day of the death of the child or orphan` AT LEAST (YMD 1978 1 1)
    AND (NOT `s 2(2) — the person is treated as having reached a specified age on a date for a provision` `any other provision` `the child's or orphan's date of birth` 18 `the day of the death of the child or orphan`)
    AND `no application had been made at the time of the death`
    AND `a date is within a time limit after a start date` `the day the application is made` `the day of the death of the child or orphan` (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 1)
    AND (   `the applicant is the person or agency having decision-making responsibility in respect of the child or orphan at the time of the death`
         OR (`there was at the time of the death no person or agency having decision-making responsibility` AND `the applicant is a person or agency that the Minister has directed`))

-- src:2038 | Benefits payable to estate or other persons
-- src:2039 | (4) Where an application is made pursuant to subsection (2) or (3), a benefit that would have been payable to a deceased person referred to in subsection (2) or a deceased child or orphan referred to in subsection (3) shall be paid to the estate or such person as may be prescribed by regulation.
@ref Act s 60(4) (src:2039)
GIVEN `the payee is the estate of the deceased person, child or orphan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payee is a person prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(4) — the benefit applied for under subsection (2) or (3) is paid to the payee` `the payee is the estate of the deceased person, child or orphan` `the payee is a person prescribed by regulation` MEANS
    -- "shall be paid to the estate or such person as may be prescribed by regulation" (reg 57, piece cr2).
    `the payee is the estate of the deceased person, child or orphan` OR `the payee is a person prescribed by regulation`

-- src:2040 | Application deemed to have been received on date of death
-- src:2041 | (5) Any application made pursuant to subsection (2) or (3) is deemed to have been received
-- src:2042 | (a) on the date of the death of a person who, prior to his death, would have been entitled, on approval of an application, to payment of a benefit under this Act; or
-- src:2043 | (b) on the date of the death of a child or an orphan referred to in subsection (3) if the person or agency having decision-making responsibility in respect of the child or orphan did not make an application prior to the death of the child or orphan.
@ref Act s 60(5) (src:2041-2043)
GIVEN `the application is made under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or agency having decision-making responsibility did not make an application prior to the death of the child or orphan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 60(5) — the day an application made under subsection (2) or (3) is deemed to have been received` `the application is made under subsection (2)` `the application is made under subsection (3)` `the person or agency having decision-making responsibility did not make an application prior to the death of the child or orphan` `the day of the death` MEANS
    -- (a): the date of the death of the person who would have been entitled; (b): the date of the death of the child
    -- or orphan, if no application was made before.
    IF `the application is made under subsection (2)` OR (`the application is made under subsection (3)` AND `the person or agency having decision-making responsibility did not make an application prior to the death of the child or orphan`)
    THEN JUST `the day of the death`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 60(6) and (7) -- how the application is made and decided`

-- src:2044 | How application to be made
-- src:2045 | (6) An application for a benefit shall be made to the Minister in prescribed manner and at the prescribed location.
@ref Act s 60(6) (src:2045)
GIVEN `the application is made to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made at the prescribed location` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(6) — an application for a benefit is made as the Act requires` `the application is made to the Minister` `the application is made in the prescribed manner` `the application is made at the prescribed location` MEANS
    -- The prescribed manner is writing (reg 43(1), piece cr2).
        `the application is made to the Minister`
    AND `the application is made in the prescribed manner`
    AND `the application is made at the prescribed location`

-- src:2046 | Consideration of application and approval by Minister
-- src:2047 | (7) The Minister shall forthwith on receiving an application for a benefit consider it and may approve payment of the benefit and determine the amount thereof payable under this Act or may determine that no benefit is payable, and he shall thereupon in writing notify the applicant of his decision.
@ref Act s 60(7) (src:2047)
GIVEN `the Minister has received an application for a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(7) — the Minister must consider the application at once and notify the applicant in writing of the decision` `the Minister has received an application for a benefit` MEANS
    -- The Minister then "may approve payment of the benefit and determine the amount thereof ... or may determine that
    -- no benefit is payable": the decision is the Minister's; the duty to consider forthwith and to notify in writing is
    -- what the applicant is owed.
    `the Minister has received an application for a benefit`

§§ `Section 60(8) to (11.1) -- incapacity`

-- src:2048 | Incapacity
-- src:2049 | (8) Where an application for a benefit is made on behalf of a person and the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of that person, that the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application on the person’s own behalf on the day on which the application was actually made, the Minister may deem the application to have been made in the month preceding the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid or in the month that the Minister considers the person’s last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced, whichever is the later.
@ref Act s 60(8) (src:2049)
GIVEN `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated` IS A DATE
      `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a regulation prescribes otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made on behalf of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of the person, that the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application on the person's own behalf on the day on which the application was actually made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid` IS A DATE
      `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 60(8) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made on behalf of the person to have been made` `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated` `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` `a regulation prescribes otherwise` `the application is made on behalf of the person` `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of the person, that the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application on the person's own behalf on the day on which the application was actually made` `the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid` `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced` MEANS
    -- NOTHING: the Minister has no power to deem. "the month preceding the first month in which the relevant benefit
    -- could have commenced to be paid, or the month ... incapacity [is considered] to have commenced, whichever is the later".
    IF   `s 60(11) — subsections (8) to (10) apply to the individual` `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated`
     AND `s 60(10) — the period of incapacity counts` `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` `a regulation prescribes otherwise`
     AND `the application is made on behalf of the person`
     AND `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of the person, that the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application on the person's own behalf on the day on which the application was actually made`
    THEN JUST (`cp4 the later of two months` (`add months` (`the month of a date` `the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid`) (0 MINUS 1)) `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2050 | Idem
-- src:2051 | (9) Where an application for a benefit is made by or on behalf of a person and the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of that person, that
-- src:2052 | (a) the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application before the day on which the application was actually made,
-- src:2053 | (b) the person had ceased to be so incapable before that day, and
-- src:2054 | (c) the application was made
-- src:2055 | (i) within the period that begins on the day on which that person had ceased to be so incapable and that comprises the same number of days, not exceeding twelve months, as in the period of incapacity, or
-- src:2056 | (ii) where the period referred to in subparagraph (i) comprises fewer than thirty days, not more than one month after the month in which that person had ceased to be so incapable,
-- src:2057 | the Minister may deem the application to have been made in the month preceding the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid or in the month that the Minister considers the person’s last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced, whichever is the later.
@ref Act s 60(9) (src:2051-2057)
GIVEN `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated` IS A DATE
      `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a regulation prescribes otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of the person, that the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application before the day on which it was actually made, and had ceased to be so incapable before that day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable` IS A DATE
      `the number of days in the period of incapacity` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the application was actually made or the information actually received` IS A DATE
      `the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid` IS A DATE
      `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 60(9) — the month in which the Minister may deem an application made by or on behalf of the person after incapacity has ceased to have been made` `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated` `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` `a regulation prescribes otherwise` `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of the person, that the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application before the day on which it was actually made, and had ceased to be so incapable before that day` `the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable` `the number of days in the period of incapacity` `the day on which the application was actually made or the information actually received` `the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid` `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced` MEANS
    IF   `s 60(11) — subsections (8) to (10) apply to the individual` `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated`
     AND `s 60(10) — the period of incapacity counts` `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` `a regulation prescribes otherwise`
     AND `the Minister is satisfied, on the basis of evidence provided by or on behalf of the person, that the person had been incapable of forming or expressing an intention to make an application before the day on which it was actually made, and had ceased to be so incapable before that day`
     AND `cp4 the application was made within the period after incapacity ceased` `the day on which the person ceased to be so incapable` `the number of days in the period of incapacity` `the day on which the application was actually made or the information actually received`
    THEN JUST (`cp4 the later of two months` (`add months` (`the month of a date` `the first month in which the relevant benefit could have commenced to be paid`) (0 MINUS 1)) `the month that the Minister considers the person's last relevant period of incapacity to have commenced`)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2058 | Period of incapacity
-- src:2059 | (10) For the purposes of subsections (8) and (9), a period of incapacity must be a continuous period except as otherwise prescribed.
@ref Act s 60(10) (src:2059)
GIVEN `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a regulation prescribes otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(10) — the period of incapacity counts` `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` `a regulation prescribes otherwise` MEANS
    `the period of incapacity is a continuous period` OR `a regulation prescribes otherwise`

-- src:2060 | Application
-- src:2061 | (11) Subsections (8) to (10) apply only to individuals who were incapacitated on or after January 1, 1991.
@ref Act s 60(11) (src:2061)
GIVEN `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(11) — subsections (8) to (10) apply to the individual` `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated` MEANS
    `the last day on which the individual was incapacitated` AT LEAST (YMD 1991 1 1)

-- src:2062 | Disabled contributor’s child’s benefit application
-- src:2063 | (11.1) If an application for a disability pension or a post-retirement disability benefit is deemed, under subsection (8) or (9), to have been made in a month that precedes the month in which it was actually made, the Minister may also deem the application for a disabled contributor’s child’s benefit to have been made on behalf of the contributor’s child in that same month.
@ref Act s 60(11.1) (src:2063)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of benefit`
      `the month to which the application for the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit is deemed to have been made under subsection (8) or (9)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the month in which that application was actually made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 60(11.1) — the month in which the Minister may also deem the application for a disabled contributor's child's benefit to have been made` kind `the month to which the application for the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit is deemed to have been made under subsection (8) or (9)` `the month in which that application was actually made` MEANS
    -- NOTHING: no power to deem (the application is not for a disability pension or post-retirement disability
    -- benefit, or it was not deemed made in an earlier month).
    CONSIDER `the month to which the application for the disability pension or post-retirement disability benefit is deemed to have been made under subsection (8) or (9)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST deemed THEN
        IF   (CONSIDER kind
              WHEN `a disability pension` THEN TRUE
              WHEN `a post-retirement disability benefit` THEN TRUE
              OTHERWISE FALSE)
         AND (`the month of a date` deemed LESS THAN `the month of a date` `the month in which that application was actually made`)
        THEN JUST (`the month of a date` deemed)
        ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 60(12) -- making a claim or providing information in person`

-- src:2064 | Making claim or providing information in person
-- src:2065 | (12) The Minister may require an applicant or other person or a group or class of persons to be at a suitable place at a suitable time in order to make an application for benefits in person or to provide additional information about an application.
@ref Act s 60(12) (src:2065)
GIVEN `the Minister requires the person, or a group or class of persons that includes the person, to be at a suitable place at a suitable time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is to make an application for benefits in person or to provide additional information about an application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 60(12) — the person must be at the place and time the Minister requires` `the Minister requires the person, or a group or class of persons that includes the person, to be at a suitable place at a suitable time` `the purpose is to make an application for benefits in person or to provide additional information about an application` MEANS
    -- What is "suitable" is the Minister's judgment; the rule takes it as the first input.
        `the Minister requires the person, or a group or class of persons that includes the person, to be at a suitable place at a suitable time`
    AND `the purpose is to make an application for benefits in person or to provide additional information about an application`

§ `Section 61 -- interim benefit`

-- src:2066 | Approval of interim benefit
-- src:2067 | 61 (1) Where application is made for a benefit and payment of the benefit would be approved except that the amount of the benefit cannot be finally calculated at the time the approval would otherwise be given, the Minister may approve payment of an interim benefit in such amount as he may fix and payment of the interim benefit may be made in a like manner as if the benefit had been approved.
@ref Act s 61(1) (src:2067)
GIVEN `an application is made for a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `payment of the benefit would be approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of the benefit cannot be finally calculated at the time the approval would otherwise be given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 61(1) — the Minister may approve payment of an interim benefit` `an application is made for a benefit` `payment of the benefit would be approved` `the amount of the benefit cannot be finally calculated at the time the approval would otherwise be given` MEANS
    -- The amount of the interim benefit is "such amount as he may fix": the Minister's decision, not derived here.
        `an application is made for a benefit`
    AND `payment of the benefit would be approved`
    AND `the amount of the benefit cannot be finally calculated at the time the approval would otherwise be given`

-- src:2068 | Adjustment to be made when benefit subsequently approved
-- src:2069 | (2) Where an interim benefit has been paid under subsection (1) and payment of a benefit is subsequently approved,
-- src:2070 | (a) if the amount of the interim benefit was less than the amount of the benefit subsequently approved, the beneficiary shall be paid the additional amount that he would have been paid if the benefit had been approved at the time the interim benefit was approved; and
@ref Act s 61(2)(a) (src:2070)
GIVEN `the amount of the interim benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the benefit subsequently approved` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 61(2)(a) — the additional amount the beneficiary is paid` `the amount of the interim benefit` `the amount of the benefit subsequently approved` MEANS
    -- "the beneficiary shall be paid the additional amount that he would have been paid if the benefit had been
    -- approved at the time the interim benefit was approved": the difference, when the interim benefit was less.
    max 0 (`the amount of the benefit subsequently approved` MINUS `the amount of the interim benefit`)

-- src:2071 | (b) if the amount of the interim benefit exceeded the amount of the benefit subsequently approved, the amount paid in excess thereof shall be deducted from subsequent payments of the benefit or otherwise recovered in such manner as the Minister may direct.
@ref Act s 61(2)(b) (src:2071)
GIVEN `the amount of the interim benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the benefit subsequently approved` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 61(2)(b) — the excess that is deducted from subsequent payments or otherwise recovered` `the amount of the interim benefit` `the amount of the benefit subsequently approved` MEANS
    -- "deducted from subsequent payments of the benefit or otherwise recovered in such manner as the Minister may direct".
    max 0 (`the amount of the interim benefit` MINUS `the amount of the benefit subsequently approved`)

§ `Section 62 -- when payment is made`

-- src:2072 | Where payment approved after month of commencement
-- src:2073 | 62 (1) Payment of a benefit for each month shall be made at such time during the month as the Minister directs, except that, where payment of a benefit is approved after the end of the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part, monthly payments of the benefit shall be made for months commencing with the month following the month in which payment of the benefit is approved and payments of the benefit for months preceding that month for which the benefit is payable under this Part shall be paid in one sum during that month.
@ref Act s 62(1) (src:2073)
GIVEN `the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part` IS A DATE
      `the month in which payment of the benefit is approved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 62(1) — payment is approved after the end of the month for which the first payment is payable` `the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part` `the month in which payment of the benefit is approved` MEANS
    `the month of a date` `the month in which payment of the benefit is approved` GREATER THAN `the month of a date` `the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part`

-- src:2073 | 62 (1) Payment of a benefit for each month shall be made at such time during the month as the Minister directs, except that, where payment of a benefit is approved after the end of the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part, monthly payments of the benefit shall be made for months commencing with the month following the month in which payment of the benefit is approved and payments of the benefit for months preceding that month for which the benefit is payable under this Part shall be paid in one sum during that month.
@ref Act s 62(1) (src:2073)
GIVEN `the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part` IS A DATE
      `the month in which payment of the benefit is approved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 62(1) — the month from which monthly payments are made` `the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part` `the month in which payment of the benefit is approved` MEANS
    IF `s 62(1) — payment is approved after the end of the month for which the first payment is payable` `the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part` `the month in which payment of the benefit is approved`
    THEN `the month following the month of a date` `the month in which payment of the benefit is approved`
    ELSE `the month of a date` `the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part`

-- src:2073 | 62 (1) Payment of a benefit for each month shall be made at such time during the month as the Minister directs, except that, where payment of a benefit is approved after the end of the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part, monthly payments of the benefit shall be made for months commencing with the month following the month in which payment of the benefit is approved and payments of the benefit for months preceding that month for which the benefit is payable under this Part shall be paid in one sum during that month.
@ref Act s 62(1) (src:2073)
GIVEN `the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part` IS A DATE
      `the month in which payment of the benefit is approved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 62(1) — the number of months for which payment is made in one sum` `the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part` `the month in which payment of the benefit is approved` MEANS
    -- "payments of the benefit for months preceding that month for which the benefit is payable under this Part shall
    -- be paid in one sum during that month": the months from the first month payable up to the month before the
    -- month from which monthly payments are made, which is paid in the month that follows the month of approval.
    IF `s 62(1) — payment is approved after the end of the month for which the first payment is payable` `the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part` `the month in which payment of the benefit is approved`
    THEN `the number of months from the month of one date to the month of another` `the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part` (`s 62(1) — the month from which monthly payments are made` `the month for which the first payment of the benefit is payable under this Part` `the month in which payment of the benefit is approved`)
    ELSE 0

-- src:2074 | When benefit deemed to have become payable
-- src:2075 | (2) For the purposes of this Act, where a benefit is payable under this Part commencing with any month, the benefit shall be deemed to have become payable at the beginning of that month.
@ref Act s 62(2) (src:2075)
GIVEN `the month with which the benefit is payable under this Part commences` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 62(2) — the day a benefit is deemed to have become payable` `the month with which the benefit is payable under this Part commences` MEANS
    `the month of a date` `the month with which the benefit is payable under this Part commences`
